# C051 — OSB-MANIFEST PLATFORM GENERATOR + autotoolfactory (architecture-only; operator chose "new higher-level manifest"
# + "record it, build later"). Operator vision: a separate package where a user writes ONE OSB-style contract that
# provisions the ENTIRE Hono backend by adding the shadcn registry components (C050); LEAVE toolfactory alone; create a new
# ~/apps/autotoolfactory generated from a single document at full toolfactory parity MINUS the product routes (transcribe/
# subtitle/convert). Sits ATOP C050 (registry) + C047 (provision). NOT a contract facet.

# THE APEX OF C047+C050 fused under one author document. THE MANIFEST (new higher-level schema, definePlatform): services
# {auth/keys/credits/billing/cost/logs/stores/erasure/journeys/audit} + per-service opts + infra target; COMPILES DOWN to
# two IRs — (a) a C047 provision.config (merged InstanceSpec[] from each service's provision fragment) + (b) the ordered
# shadcn-add list (each service's registry component). Manifest = ergonomic surface; provision.config = compiled IR, so
# NOTHING in C047 changes. THE CATALOG (the one new artifact = OSB offerings): service-id -> {component: shadcn ref,
# requires: module-deps, npm: hybrid logic dep, provision:(opts)->InstanceSpec[], env}. THE GENERATOR (new pkg, thin over
# C047 apply + shadcn): read manifest -> topo-resolve vs catalog -> per service `shadcn add` (owned code) + collect
# provision(opts) -> merge fragments -> provision.config -> @suluk/provision generate/migrate/apply. The ONLY novel step
# over C047 is per-service CODE materialization; all infra is C047. autotoolfactory = the generator's OUTPUT repo (Hono
# backend, toolfactory parity minus product), parity MEASURED by diffing routes/schema/journeys vs toolfactory.
claim platform_generator_osb_manifest_compiles_to_provision_plus_shadcn: Bool @>=0.45 = True
falsified_when platform_generator_osb_manifest_compiles_to_provision_plus_shadcn == False

# C051 SUPERSEDES C049 + the SAFETY WIN + the dependency chain. "Leave toolfactory alone" RETIRES C049's dangerous path
# (migrating LIVE credits/billing/keys in a running app = a money-cutover); instead author the registry components FRESH +
# GENERATE a clean app, using toolfactory as the parity ORACLE (diff target) not a migration subject. So the money modules
# (credits/keys/billing/payments) are proven in a FRESH generated app (journeys + parity-diff), never touching a live money
# path — strictly safer than C049 Phase C. C049 SUPERSEDED. HARD DEPENDENCY CHAIN: C050 registry components -> C051
# generator -> autotoolfactory (the generator can only add components that EXIST). So NOTHING builds until >=1 C050 component
# is real; first build = a VERTICAL SLICE (one service -> generate -> one component + provision fragment -> running stub) to
# prove the pipeline before scaling to ~10 modules. The generator's new code is SMALL (apply + shadcn step + a catalog
# resolver); the BULK of effort is authoring the ~10 C050 components faithfully vs toolfactory. OPEN: generator name,
# manifest format (.ts definePlatform vs YAML), catalog home, generated-and-committed vs on-demand. Backend-first; web/UI
# parity is Phase 2. DESIGNED-not-built + depends-on-unbuilt-C050 => ceiling 0.45.
claim platform_generator_supersedes_c049_fresh_parity_app_safer_money: Bool @>=0.45 = True
falsified_when platform_generator_supersedes_c049_fresh_parity_app_safer_money == False

# C051 BUILD #1 — @suluk/platform (the generator) built 2026-07-01. manifest.ts: definePlatform({name, registry, services})
# — the higher-level author document. catalog.ts: CATALOG (the OSB offerings — service-id -> {mount: base|middleware|route
# with symbol/path/from, provision:{symbol,from}}) for the 6 registry modules + orderServices (app+auth first, then
# manifest order). merge.ts: mergeProvision(fragments[][]) — combines same-ref instances (every module targets ref "db")
# into ONE, UNIONING migrations in fragment order (auth's tables first) — without it two "db" instances collide on the ref.
# plan.ts: planPlatform(manifest) PURE -> {services, adds (registry refs), entry (the wired src/index.ts: createApp() +
# mountAuthRoutes(app) + app.route per feature + export default), provisionConfig (imports each fragment + mergeProvision)}.
# generate.ts: generatePlatform(manifest, {run, write, log}) — the impure shell: run bunx shadcn add per service (fetches
# owned code + deps + registryDeps), write the entry + provision.config; STOPS short of provision apply (live infra op).
# bin/platform.ts: the CLI (Bun.spawn + fs). deps @suluk/provision. WITNESSED — platform 7 pass: plan orders app+auth-first
# + registry-ref adds; the entry wires base+auth-middleware+each-route; the provision.config imports+merges the fragments;
# unknown-service throws; mergeProvision unions same-ref migrations in order + keeps distinct refs; generate runs an add
# per service then writes 2 files. tsc clean. The generator new code is SMALL (a catalog resolver + a shadcn step + the
# merge) exactly as C051 predicted. REMAINING: scaffold ~/apps/autotoolfactory + run it (shadcn adds are network+npm; a dry
# generation produces the wiring deterministically) + diff-parity vs toolfactory; provision apply is the operator's live step.
claim platform_generator_c051_build1_manifest_catalog_plan_merge_generate_built: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when platform_generator_c051_build1_manifest_catalog_plan_merge_generate_built == False

# C051 BUILD #2 — the ONE-SHOT PROVEN END-TO-END + a real bug caught live (2026-07-01). Scaffolded ~/apps/autotoolfactory
# + platform.config.ts (definePlatform services auth/credits/keys/billing/logs), ran the generator (dry) -> the wired
