# Then LIVE `bunx shadcn add MahmoodKhalil57/suluk/{auth,credits,keys,billing,logs}` PULLED ALL 20 MODULE FILES from the
# pushed public registry (app auto-resolved via registryDependencies). BUG CAUGHT LIVE (the value of a real run): shadcn
# resolves BARE registryDependencies ("app") against the DEFAULT registry ui.shadcn.com, NOT the GitHub repo -> the first
# add failed fetching app.json from ui.shadcn.com; FIX = fully-qualify registryDependencies to MahmoodKhalil57/suluk/<item>
# (all 5 items); re-pushed. SECOND fix: shadcn lands `target: provision/x.ts` under the components base (src/provision/),
# so the generated provision.config's import path was corrected to ./src/provision/<x> (catalog.from). platform 7 pass
# still green. So: ONE manifest -> the generator wired the entry + merged provision, and a single shadcn-add command pulled
# the whole backend's owned code. The one-shot autotoolfactory pipeline WORKS. REMAINING: publish @suluk/platform (the
# generated provision.config imports mergeProvision from it) so autotoolfactory installs; bun install + tsc = the parity
# signal; provision apply is the operator's live infra step.
claim platform_c051_build2_oneshot_autotoolfactory_proven_live_shadcn_add: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when platform_c051_build2_oneshot_autotoolfactory_proven_live_shadcn_add == False

# C051 BUILD #3 — the FULL 8-SERVICE one-shot regenerated + PARITY MEASURED (2026-07-01). The catalog gained the 3 new
# C050-build-4 modules (cost as a route+provision entry; journeys/audit under a NEW "dev" Mount kind = files-only, no entry
# line + no provision fragment) — so the planner's buildEntry naturally skips dev modules (no middleware/route branch
# matches) and buildProvisionConfig naturally skips them (no `.provision`), needing ZERO new plan/generate logic beyond the
# type. platform tests now 9 pass (added: cost mounts /cost + folds costProvision into mergeProvision; journeys/audit add
# shadcn refs but contribute NO entry mount + NO provision import). autotoolfactory REGENERATED from ONE manifest of 8
# services (auth/credits/keys/billing/cost/logs/journeys/audit): the updated planner emitted the wired src/index.ts (now
# with app.route("/cost", costRoutes())) + the merged provision.config (costProvision folded in, journeys/audit absent);
# live `bunx shadcn add` pulled all module files — the 3 new + the reconciled Better-Auth-v1.6.23 auth schema/provision
# (--overwrite). SHADCN-BASE FINDING (a real bug caught by the live regen): shadcn prefixes NON-src/ registry targets under
# the components base (src/), so journeys.config.ts + journeys.test.ts land as SIBLINGS in src/ (fix: import ./journeys.config
# not ../) and scripts/conformance.ts lands at src/scripts/ (fix: conformance uses node:fs not the Bun global so it
# typechecks under a node-types tsconfig). PARITY SIGNAL: `bunx tsc --noEmit` = 0 errors in the generated src/ + config
# (the lone error is a pre-existing @suluk/openapi-compat transitive-SOURCE nit, unrelated); tsconfig excludes
# src/**/*.test.ts (the bun:test journeys harness runs under `bun test`, not the Worker build); `bun test` = 1 skip (the
# harness skips until a contract exists) + 0 fail. So the one-shot pipeline holds at FULL toolfactory-minus-product parity:
# one document → generator → 8-service Hono backend, generated code typechecks clean. autotoolfactory is a LOCAL parity
# oracle (no remote). REMAINING: republish @suluk/platform (0.1.1, the updated catalog) so the one-shot runs from the
# INSTALLED generator not the source planner; provision apply is the operator's live infra step.
claim platform_c051_build3_full_8service_oneshot_regenerated_parity_typechecks_clean: Bool @>=0.62 = True
falsified_when platform_c051_build3_full_8service_oneshot_regenerated_parity_typechecks_clean == False

